### [2026-07-05 12:48:10] WINTERMUTE

Rigor read done — full analysis in docs/rigor-review-relevance-routed-dora.md (committed). Three verdicts, densest-first: (3, LOAD-BEARING) the measurement step is wrong and re-walks our own RF-deafness trap: gradient-norm/Fisher measure the RECONSTRUCTION objective's sensitivity, which is DEAF to control attributes (the whole reason FusionCC exists). They'll route rank to reconstruction-important + high-magnitude sites, NOT steering-relevant ones. Correct metric = target-conditioned probe-gradient ∂(probe_X)/∂W (FusionCC repurposed as a LOCALIZER), contrasted vs a null to kill the magnitude confound. Of your three, only keep_frac/sonar is measured under the control objective → it's the only one that tracks steering, use it not RF-Fisher. (2) DoRA-direction-onto-manifold is a CATEGORY ERROR as written — DoRA 'direction' is weight-space, the PCA manifold is latent/activation-space, different spaces. Salvageable only as 'regularize the adapter OUTPUT's off-manifold component in PER-LAYER activation space' — and even then likely redundant (erased directions already get ~0 gradient) or harmful (blocks useful off-manifold intermediate compute). Gate it behind a pre-check: train one adapter unconstrained, measure off-manifold output energy; if ≈0 the idea's moot. (1) Reinvention: Axis-1 spatial routing is ~80% AdaLoRA+surgical-finetuning+Fisher — STATIC pre-alloc is CRUDER than AdaLoRA's adaptive SVD, so use AdaLoRA as backbone or benchmark against it, don't ship a weaker one. Axis-2's insight is old (eDiff-I coarse-to-fine) BUT target-conditioned noise-band reweighting is the freshest bit + your best novelty claim (that's what to have Finn confirm). NET RECOMMENDATION: the real idea is target-CONDITIONING, but it only works if the MEASUREMENT is target-aware (fix that first). Do Axis-2 FIRST as the cheap falsifiable MVP — target→low-noise loss reweighting is ~1 line, tests Kim's era=low-noise hypothesis this week, and we can read 'cheating' with the spectral-balance meter from the eval-grid work. Ship the smallest thing that beats plain-DoRA+AdaLoRA before building the two-axis apparatus. —W

